Implemented a staged causally censored graph-boosting pipeline for rel-event/users-birthyear.
Added strict compact friendship extraction, demographic and causal target encodings, robust one-hop and two-hop label features, friend demographics, and exact-time activity profiles with fixed signed event projections.
Added expanding forward-fold LightGBM/CatBoost training, statistically gated OOF ensembling, causal soft-neighbor residuals, confidence gating, Correct & Smooth, internal clipping selection, and strict Model A/Model B prediction separation.
Added content-keyed shared feature/component caches, artifact registration, measurement profile, time allocation, per-stratum diagnostics, and contract checks.
Tested and rejected an additional winsorized demographic-residual/family-gap friend-label block because its latest forward fold deteriorated; the final code retains the simpler stable block.
Added a train-only feature-block selector that omits sparse activity columns from both boosters after the removal improved the forward-fold mean and latest fold for both model families; causal activity matrices remain built and diagnosed.
Tested and rejected explicit isolated-user shrinkage toward causal locale/gender/country priors because every blend degraded both mean and latest-fold R².
Tested and rejected a count-gated robust hard-friend post-blend because its small mean gain did not clear pooled uncertainty.
Tested and rejected causal rolling global/locale cohort priors because aggregate OOF and the latest CatBoost fold deteriorated.
Tested and rejected causal friend-demographic target-prior aggregates because their mean gain did not exceed one pooled standard error.
Added a model-specific selector retaining friend demographics for LightGBM while omitting them from CatBoost after CatBoost improved on the first and latest forward folds and tied the middle fold.
No external datasets or pretrained models were used.
RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
